    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0336" n="170" xml:id="pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/240</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-12T18:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 12, 1917, 6 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram of January 8, 5 p.m.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d228-f1"/> I have
                    informally suggested to Japanese Minister possibility of cooperation between
                    American and Japanese interests in the construction of railways in Manchuria
                    recalling to him the existence of American rights in that regard.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
